# Approved request
Implement Work parallel execution with P1-P5 admission, natural-language policy changes, review/rework, cleanup verification, Claude-first/Codex adapter boundary; deploy to nightly. SSE configuration accepts an external idle-discovery instruction. Test default: search Walkie unresolved items by priority then latest creation time. Approval/block waits must include independent-item pickup guidance without approving blocked work.

# Latest deletion rule
Worktrees may be removed only after their HEAD is verified on a remote ref OR the user explicitly approved deletion of that exact target. Dirty/active/unowned targets remain blocked regardless. No force removal, no automatic branch deletion.

# Isolation
Base: remote nightly 4758efb. Dedicated feature/work-parallel-20261103 worktree. Root checkout has unrelated statusline changes and remains untouched. No live router restart or live test sweep.

# Verification so far
24 focused unittest tests passed across discovery policy, external SSE settings and existing concurrent Work mod gates (including two new approval/block discovery scenarios). Real local Git worktree cleanup: five cases passed, including pushed, unpushed, explicit approval and dirty retention. Parallel engine agent reported 35 tests; parent rerun after aligning Korean default: 34 pass, one outdated default-text assertion failed and corrected, rerun pending.

# Not yet verified
Actual Claude fork execution/host identity, full coordinator integration, real menu actions and screenshots, nightly publication. No deployment claim yet.

# Parent verification update
- 163 scheduler/MCP/tree/store/discovery/cleanup tests + 115 subtests passed in isolated config.
- 33 launch-environment/menu regression tests + 63 subtests passed.
- Native fork probe 81ab073d: actual Claude CLI agent.spawn observed fork=true,type=fork, exit0.
- Integrated native mod E2E is NOT passing yet: actual compiler rejects duplicate/generic middleware hooks. Static hook composition is being fixed and re-tested; no nightly push has occurred.
- Latest-first uses immutable created_at on new tree nodes; older nodes migrate with the only available historical timestamp, updated_at.
- Deletion tests use owned temporary Git repositories and local bare remotes; no user worktree has been removed.

# Final integration checks (2026-11-03)
- Focused isolated regression: 204 passed, 188 subtests passed. After cleanup review: 58 scheduler/cleanup/MCP cases passed.
- Native packaged-mod CLI run parallel-e2e-1115379f: default off, configure, reserve, bind, child result and hard-cap rejection all observed; no hooks-module compiler errors. Provider is an owned loopback fake gateway, not production LLM behavior.
- Plugin validate passed; catalog icon warning only. Repository ruff check passed before final cleanup change; rerun required.
- Review found cleanup-before-CAS and absent workspace ownership binding. Cleanup now executes only after transition validation under the CAS lock. Host workspace ownership/idle proof is required; the current native adapter does not expose it, so automatic workspace removal remains fail-closed. Pushed/explicit-approved deletion is verified in the isolated Git fixture with supplied authenticated host bindings, not claimed as a live native path.
- Native adapter supports scheduling and result identity. Codex is explicitly unsupported; usage unknown blocks P2-P5. Review dispatch remains coordinator-driven.
- Raw isolated run directories and credentials remain local and are excluded from commit/package. Compact summary is evidence/integration-summary.json.

# Final regression and menu evidence
- Final focused run: 208 passed, 188 subtests passed; repository ruff passed.
- Actual isolated Windows menu: max_active=2 and P2=0.7 persisted via keyboard interaction. Console text and screenshots in evidence/menu-ui; verification.json confirms ledger values.

# CI publication correction
Initial publish run 41639128314 failed before npm publication: two new tests imported pytest although CI uses dependency-free unittest; architecture test detected work_parallel -> work_discovery -> work_parallel_mcp -> work_parallel cycle. Shared instruction moved into leaf work_parallel_defaults.py. Both pytest modules converted to unittest preserving 53 expanded cases (all passed). Remaining focused unittest modules: 155 passed. Import-graph architecture contract: passed. No test or publication gate bypassed.

# Published nightly verification
307ceec published as 0.2.51-nightly.20261103-131045.307ceec. Publish run 41640117627 and CI 41640117708 both success. Registry gitHead matches exact commit; npm pack downloaded tarball and verified scheduler/defaults/MCP/discovery/cleanup modules and native mod presence. No live session restarted or local install overwritten.

# Scope reopened: all remaining automation and crash recovery
User requested completing all remaining parts and recovering fork work after parent forced exit. Current release does not guarantee this: native adapter uses process-local pending/bound Maps; durable ledger alone cannot restart a native child. Investigating official/native resume and workspace observations before implementing. Recovery must reconcile before dispatch and never treat an absent list row as proof of termination. Owned isolated process tests only; no production forced termination.

# Remaining implementation verification
- Actual forced-kill/restart recovery passed repeatedly: same parent session, persisted native agent name/ID, same worker and single lease result (latest owned-worktree run crash-resume-dbc5991d). Resume permitted only during exact SendMessage coordinator call; pause/approval preserved. A waiting_input worker is not auto-resumed.
- Automatic read-only reviewer dispatch verified in real native CLI run parallel-e2e-66fb183e; use $.agent.spawn (native host rejects $.tool.call Agent). Submitted idle workers release slots before review. Reviewer receives worker artifact and workspace path.
- Runtime-owned worktree manifest verifies exact lease/repo/host/branch ownership; native cwd is supplied before launch. Windows Git children must use DEVNULL stdin in threaded MCP handler. Worktree tests passed17.
- Durable pickup ingestion implemented and exposed as work_discovery_pickup: planning-only registration, source/item dedup, scope/status/priority/latest validation, cooldown and concurrency tests passed11. No actual authenticated Walkie item-search connector exists in this runtime/session; production external search remains unverified and must not be called complete.
